## Rename documentation/ → docs/ (single canonical docs root)

Context: the repository had two parallel documentation trees — the historical
`documentation/` (Help Center markdown, Sphinx sources, INFO/README) and a
newer `docs/superpowers/` created by the writing-plans skill default. After
first consolidating everything under `documentation/`, the decision was
reversed to standardize on `docs/`, aligning with the `.cursorrules` "in /docs"
wording and the superpowers skill default. The whole tree was renamed and every
functional reference updated; historical audit files (changelogs, releases,
superpowers plan/spec bodies) were intentionally left untouched.

Changes:

1. documentation/ → docs/
   `git mv` of the entire tree (192 tracked files) so history is preserved.
2. src/api/routers/internal/help.py
   Help Center now resolves `<repo>/docs` (was `<repo>/documentation`); docstrings
   and the missing-dir audit warning updated.
3. databricks.yml, .databricksignore
   Bundle sync now ships `docs/**`; excludes point at `docs/sphinx/_build/` and
   `.doctrees/`. Removed the stale wholesale `docs/` exclusion (former GitHub
   Pages marketing site) that would otherwise strip the Help Center from the
   deployed bundle.
4. ci/build_docs.sh, pyproject.toml, Makefile, scripts/deploy.sh,
   scripts/_internal/_deploy-preflight.sh
   Sphinx source dir, mypy/coverage excludes, and deploy-checklist pointers
   repointed to `docs/`.
5. src/front/static/global/js/help-docs.js, src/front/templates/settings.html
   GitHub blob links and the Help Center path label repointed to `docs/`; the
   JS asset normaliser keeps a legacy `documentation/` strip for old links.
6. tests/units/api/test_help_api.py
   Fixed the deploy-bundle guard tests for the inverted semantics — `docs/` must
   NOT be excluded — and the asset-ref normaliser's legacy fallback.
7. .cursor/07-project-conventions.mdc
   Documented `docs/` as the single canonical docs root and that superpowers
   plans/specs live under `docs/superpowers/`.

