## Deploy hygiene: ship only the Help Center runtime set from docs/

Context: after the documentation/ → docs/ rename, the bundle synced all of
`docs/**` (only the Sphinx build output was excluded). That shipped internal-only
content — planning artifacts, Sphinx sources, diagrams, demo assets and
non-catalogued guides — to the Databricks App. The Help Center only serves a
fixed catalogue of `docs/*.md` plus `docs/images/` and `docs/screenshots/`, so
everything else under docs/ is dead weight in the deployed bundle.

Changes:

1. databricks.yml
   Replaced the two Sphinx-build excludes with a tighter set: exclude
   `docs/sphinx/`, `docs/superpowers/`, `docs/diagrams/`, `docs/pr47-neo4j-demo/`
   and the five non-catalogued markdown files (DEPLOY_CHECKLIST, PR_REVIEW_CHECKLIST,
   dab-reference, sizing, uc-mcp-connection-genie-one). Only the catalogued
   Help Center docs + images/ + screenshots/ now ship.
2. .databricksignore
   Mirrored the same exclusions so both bundle-sync mechanisms agree.
3. tests/units/api/test_help_api.py
   Added `test_bundle_excludes_non_runtime_docs` — asserts the internal docs/
   content is excluded in both databricks.yml and .databricksignore, and that no
   catalogued Help Center doc is excluded by its docs/<file> path.

